# lamu: ChargingControl (vendor.lineage.health-service.default, TOGGLE mode)
# needs RW access to /sys/devices/platform/charger/enable_charger to
# stop/resume charging (writing 0 stops it, writing 1 resumes it --
# confirmed live on hardware, stable 15s+, battery/status flips to
# "Not charging" and stays there). This is the real hardware charge
# enable/disable (DEVICE_ATTR_RW(enable_charger) in mtk_charger.c,
# platform device "charger"), not a power_supply class property.
#
# mtk-master-charger/input_current_limit (sysfs_batteryinfo type) was
# tried first since it is RW and DAC-reachable with just a chown, but it
# does NOT actually work for this: the charger algorithm thread folds it
# into its own current calculation every cycle and silently reverts an
# external write of 0 back to the previous value within ~1s -- looks
# like a success (write succeeds, no error), charging never actually
# stops. enable_charger does not have this problem: it directly calls
# charger_dev_enable() and the algorithm thread respects the flag.
allow hal_lineage_health_default vendor_sysfs_mtk_charger_enable:file rw_file_perms;
